==============================Immutable Data Types==================

Immutable objects cannot be changed in place after creation. Any modification operation creates an entirely new object in memory.

        Strings (str): Text sequences, e.g., "hello".

        Integers (int): Whole numbers, e.g., 42.

        Floats (float): Floating-point numbers, e.g., 3.14.

        Booleans (bool): True or False values, e.g., True.

        Tuples (tuple): Ordered, immutable sequences of items, e.g., (1, 2, 3).

        Frozensets (frozenset): Immutable versions of sets, e.g., frozenset([1, 2]).

        Bytes (bytes): Immutable sequence of raw bytes, e.g., b"hello".

================================== Mutable Data Types===================================

Mutable objects can have their values, elements, or internal state modified in place without changing their memory address.

        Lists (list): Ordered, changeable sequences, e.g., [1, 2, 3].

        Dictionaries (dict): Key-value mappings, e.g., {"key": "value"}.

        Sets (set): Unordered collections of unique elements, e.g., {1, 2, 3}.

        Bytearrays (bytearray): Mutable sequence of raw bytes, e.g., bytearray(b"hello").



#### Stage 1: Core Calculation Engine

Build pure, isolated evaluation logic (functions handling math strings, safe execution, and basic error handling).

Define explicit type annotations for inputs (str) and outputs (float / custom result types).

#### Stage 2: Validation & Error Handling

Implement strict input validation (handling division by zero, unbalanced parentheses, invalid syntax).

Introduce custom Python exceptions (CalculatorError, InvalidExpressionError).

#### Stage 3: Advanced Math Extensions

Add support for math constants (e, pi) and trigonometric functions (sin, cos).

Handle degree vs. radian conversions cleanly.

#### Stage 4: CLI Interface & Interactive Loop

Build the user-facing terminal interface loop (prompting input, formatting outputs, handling DEL and C actions).

Wire everything together cleanly with strict mypy compliance.